 "spec": "HALDEN COURIERS: DOMESTIC TARIFF (edition 9)\n\nAll prices are in cents. Apply the sections in order.\n\n\u00a71 Delivery times. Zone A: next working day. Zone B: two working days. Zone C: three to five working days.\n\n\u00a72 Weight. Weights are always rounded upward to a whole kilogram, never to the nearest; the minimum is 1 kg.\n\n\u00a73 Reclassification. A DOCUMENT whose rounded actual weight exceeds 1 kg is treated as a PARCEL for all purposes in this tariff.\n\n\u00a74 Chargeable weight. For a PARCEL, the chargeable weight is the greater of its actual weight and its volumetric weight, where volumetric weight = length x width x height in cm / 4000. Each is rounded up separately before the two are compared. A DOCUMENT is always charged on its actual weight only.\n\n\u00a75 Base price. Zone A: 470 for the first kg, then 110 per further kg; Zone B: 560 for the first kg, then 240 per further kg; Zone C: 840 for the first kg, then 260 per further kg.\n\n\u00a76 Heavy items. For each chargeable kg above 6 kg, the per-kg rate is increased by 60 cents. The first 6 kg are charged at the ordinary rates.\n\n\u00a77 Definitions. 'Consignment' means one item collected from one address. 'Working day' excludes public holidays.\n\n\u00a78 Surcharges. A weekend collection (Sat/Sun) adds 20% of the base price, rounded down; the percentage is never applied to other surcharges. Postcodes that BEGIN with JL or JX are remote: add a flat 300 cents after any percentage surcharge.\n\n\u00a79 Discounts. GOLD accounts receive 15% off the base price plus any percentage surcharge (rounded down to a whole cent); flat fees are never discounted. The GOLD discount is not available on Zone A consignments.\n\n\u00a710 Cap. A DOCUMENT never costs more than 800 cents in total, after all surcharges and discounts.\n\n\u00a711 Tracking. Every consignment receives a tracking reference by email on the day of collection.\n\n\u00a712 Amendments to this edition (these override any earlier section). (a) For Zone C consignments only, the volumetric divisor is 3000 instead of the divisor stated in the chargeable-weight section. (b) A PARCEL with any one side longer than 40 cm pays a flat oversize fee of 300 cents; if two or more sides are longer than 40 cm, the fee is doubled. (c) No consignment is charged less than 570 cents in total, after all other sections (including any cap).",
